	"$comment": "The closed core vocabulary of semantic IR contract 2.0.0 construct declarations (FR-142). A module declares each construct kind as data in terms of these names; the Rust reader, the Node compiler and the Python backend read this file, and each language's parity test compares its reading to semantic-ir.schema.json. Member defaults apply to a member a declaration does not list. A member with referenceItems is a reference member whose entries name types: an empty list when the member itself names them, else the members of each item that do, an item being an element of a list member or the member's own object; a declaration constrains a reference member by the roles it admits. Each rule names the member presence it requires of the declaration, and a rule with nonEmpty also requires that list member to hold at least one item in a type; rules are listed in the order the extraction frontend decides them at an artifact. Each identity and shape requirement names the member presence a declaration of that identity or shape declares. Each flag is an optional boolean declaration member with its default: immutable states that an instance of the construct never changes once created.",
